    <section class="section" id="key-takeaways">
      <span class="section-label">Summary</span>
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

      <div class="takeaway-grid">
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>Convolution Operation</h4>
          <p>Filters slide across images extracting spatial features. Weight sharing reduces parameters. Multiple filters in each layer extract different feature types.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>Pooling Layers</h4>
          <p>Max pooling preserves sharp features and provides translation invariance. Average pooling is smoother. Global pooling reduces to single values per channel.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>CNN Architecture</h4>
          <p>Stack convolutional blocks with increasing filter counts. Use pooling to downsample. Follow with dense layers for classification. Add batch norm and dropout for regularization.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>Data Augmentation</h4>
          <p>Artificially expand training data through rotations, flips, and zooms. Essential for improving generalization with limited data.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>Feature Hierarchy</h4>
          <p>Early layers detect simple features (edges). Middle layers detect textures. Deep layers detect semantic patterns. This hierarchy emerges automatically.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>Transfer Learning</h4>
          <p>Pretrained CNNs on ImageNet transfer well to new tasks. Freeze early layers (generic features) and fine-tune later layers (task-specific) for best results.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
